{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:PredictedSpectra.AlphaEmCategoricalTraceRatio","@type":"LeanModule","name":"PredictedSpectra.AlphaEmCategoricalTraceRatio","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.GeomSum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.alpha_em_categorical_trace_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.alpha_em_categorical_trace_ratio","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/alpha-em-categorical-trace-ratio.lean#L143-L182","doc":"The categorical-trace-ratio identity:\n  α_EM = h² / (q · δ_q(T_{2,9}) · δ_q(T_{3,5}))\n\nThe proof is direct algebraic substitution in R = ℤ[q^±1, h⁻¹]:\n\n  δ_q(T_{2,9}) = q⁹ - q⁻⁹  = h · [9]_q   (q_int_mul_h_skein)\n  δ_q(T_{3,5}) = q¹⁰ - q⁻¹⁰ = h · [10]_q (q_int_mul_h_skein)\n\n  Therefore:\n  h² / (q · δ_q(T_{2,9}) · δ_q(T_{3,5}))\n   = h² / (q · (h · [9]_q) · (h · [10]_q))\n   = h² / (q · h² · [9]_q · [10]_q)\n   = 1 / (q · [9]_q · [10]_q)\n   = α_EM     (by definition)\n\nAll of that is the single division-free identity\n`delta_mul_delta_eq_h_sq_mul_q_int`; only the final division into a\nquotient needs the field.\n\n-- Ref: [leitner2026] §round-12, §round-14 of conj:e-hartree-categorical-derivation\n-- Ref: [leitner2026] prop:em-coupling-projection (the bare 1/α formula)\n-- Ref: [leitner2026] def:delta-q-decoration\n","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:alpha-em-categorical-trace-ratio","label":"prop:alpha-em-categorical-trace-ratio","md":"quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/alpha-em-categorical-trace-ratio.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.alpha_em_via_delta_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.alpha_em_via_delta_q","kind":"def","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/alpha-em-categorical-trace-ratio.lean#L134-L141","doc":"The categorical-trace-ratio expression for α_EM via the δ_q layer:\n  α_EM_via_delta_q := h² / (q · δ_q(T_{2,9}) · δ_q(T_{3,5})).\n\nThis is the round-14 algebraic refactoring of α_EM into the\nq-dimension layer.\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.alpha_em_bare","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.alpha_em_bare","kind":"def","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/alpha-em-categorical-trace-ratio.lean#L127-L132","doc":"The bare formula for α_EM as the inverse of the Bring force-\ncarrier complexity (per prop:em-coupling-projection):\n  α_EM = 1 / (q · [9]_q · [10]_q).\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.alpha_em_relation_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.alpha_em_relation_iff","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/alpha-em-categorical-trace-ratio.lean#L92-L114","doc":"**THE α_EM CATEGORICAL-TRACE-RATIO IDENTITY, division-free (R[h] form).**\n\nRather than dividing, characterise α_EM by the multiplicative relation\nit satisfies. `α` is the inverse of the Bring force-carrier complexity\niff it satisfies the δ-layer relation with an `h²` on the right:\n\n  `α · (q · [9]_q · [10]_q) = 1  ↔  α · (q · δ_q(T_{2,9}) · δ_q(T_{3,5})) = h²`.\n\nHolds over any commutative ring in which the skein parameter `h` is a\nunit. The forward direction needs no hypothesis at all; `h` invertible\nis used only to cancel `h²` in the reverse direction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.delta_mul_delta_eq_h_sq_mul_q_int","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.delta_mul_delta_eq_h_sq_mul_q_int","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/alpha-em-categorical-trace-ratio.lean#L78-L90","doc":"**The structural core of the α_EM trace-ratio identity**, stated\ndivision-free over an arbitrary commutative ring:\n\n  `δ_q(T_{2,9}) · δ_q(T_{3,5}) = h² · ([9]_q · [10]_q)`.\n\nEvery factor of `h` in the categorical (δ) layer is accounted for by\none q-integer in the Bring-complexity layer; the ratio identity below\nis nothing more than this, divided through. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.q_int_mul_h_skein","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.q_int_mul_h_skein","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/alpha-em-categorical-trace-ratio.lean#L70-L76","doc":"**The defining relation of the symmetric q-integer**, division-free:\n`[n]_q · h = qⁿ − q⁻ⁿ = δ_q(T_{2,n})`. This is `geom_sum₂_mul`, i.e.\nthe telescoping identity `(∑_{i<n} xⁱ y^{n−1−i})(x − y) = xⁿ − yⁿ`,\nwhich is pure commutative-ring algebra. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.delta_q_T_3_5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.delta_q_T_3_5","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/alpha-em-categorical-trace-ratio.lean#L60-L68","doc":"The value **assigned** to δ_q(T_{3,5}): `q^10 − q^-10 = h · [10]_q`.\n\n**This is not the trace sum (corrected 2026-11-15).** Summing the actions\nof `(σ₁σ₂)^5` over `V_(3)`, `V_(2,1)`, `V_(1,1,1)` gives\n`q^10 − 1 + q^-10`, because on the 2-dimensional `V_(2,1)` the element\n`σ₁σ₂` has eigenvalues `ω, ω²` (`ω³ = 1`) and its fifth power has trace −1.\nSo the identities below hold for this assigned value, not for a derived one.\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.delta_q_T_2_n","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.delta_q_T_2_n","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/alpha-em-categorical-trace-ratio.lean#L53-L58","doc":"The categorical trace δ_q(T_{2, n}) for the (2, n)-torus knot in\nthe H_2(q) representation, summing the contributions from the two\nirreducible Hecke representations V_(2), V_(1,1) at eigenvalues\nq^n and (-q⁻¹)^n. For n odd this simplifies to qⁿ - q⁻ⁿ.\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.q_int","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.q_int","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/alpha-em-categorical-trace-ratio.lean#L42-L51","doc":"The symmetric q-deformed integer\n\n  `[n]_q = q^(n-1) + q^(n-3) + ⋯ + q^(−(n−1)) = ∑_{i<n} qⁱ · q^(−(n−1−i))`,\n\nwritten division-free as a Laurent polynomial in `q, q⁻¹`. It satisfies\n`[n]_q · (q − q⁻¹) = qⁿ − q⁻ⁿ` (`q_int_mul_h_skein`), which was the\nprevious *definition* — a quotient, and hence meaningful only when\n`h ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.h_skein","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.h_skein","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/alpha-em-categorical-trace-ratio.lean#L39-L40","doc":"The skein parameter h := q − q⁻¹ in the substrate ring R. ","signatureChunk":0}]}